3 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389762}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "444cbb80-ae9e-5580-b9e2-09ddd926c9e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-176823" :question/problem "![](images/41/41f32abbcc3dec501392378379bceb0d1c111ab4c458d832508f20adb42451e6.png)\n\nThe shaded region above represents the truth set of a predicate $P(x),$ defined over the universal set ${R}^{2}.$ Which of the following is the truth set of $¬P(x).$" :question/worked-solution "The truth set of $¬P(x)$ is the *complement* of the truth set of $P(x):$\n\n$$\n{T}_{¬P}={\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\n$$\n\nTherefore, to get the truth set of $¬P(x),$ we take all the points that belong to $U$ and do not lie in ${T}_{p},$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/bb/bb2a35ad33731bfe5f26960a518a038b21a9445e38e3647a792326e23fd105ad.png)"}]}
